+## v10.0.7: Arc UI Context + Runtime Handshake Hotfix
+
+- Embeds Arc's real top-level Chromium host when the visible client is owned by `ArcOSBrowser.exe`, while rejecting renderer/GPU/utility helper processes.
+- Opens Arc through `ArcLauncher.exe gamecustom sto` when the dispatcher is installed, establishing the STO-specific Arc context before containment.
+- Keeps polling when the Arc dispatcher exits normally during handoff instead of treating that short-lived process as the client itself.
+- PLAY STO remains a direct UMU + GE-Proton launch, but now requires the authenticated Arc client context to be active first.
+- Arc installation uses a cross-process `.arc-install.lock` so two launcher instances cannot race UMU/pressure-vessel against the same prefix.
+- Visual Stability and the GameClient-observed launch confirmation from 10.0.4/10.0.5 remain intact.
+
 ## v10.0.6: Embedded Arc Client + Direct STO
 
 10.0.6 fixes the containment architecture after host testing showed that the prior Gamescope/STO child-window path targeted the wrong surface. STO Linux Command now forces its own GUI onto X11/XWayland when a Wayland session exposes `DISPLAY`, launches or detects the real Arc main client, identifies Arc's X11 window by `_NET_WM_PID`/`xdotool getwindowpid` plus the Arc main-process discriminator, and reparents that Arc client window into the launcher viewport. `ArcOSBrowser.exe` is never accepted as the main Arc client.
